  "description": "<p>Because the acl:default predicate means that the specified Authorization should be shared to child resources, then there is no reason to specify both of the acl:accessTo and acl:accessToClass.</p>\n\n<p>acl:accessToClass would allow you more options (see \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-2854\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-2854\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Defining acl:accessToClass without an acl:default predicate has no benefit\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10300?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-2854\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n).</p>\n\n<p>But acl:accessTo would be re-written to the child objects URI, voiding any acl:accessToClass statements.</p>\n\n<p>ie.</p>\n\n<p>/rest/test_object</p>\n\n<p>&lt;&gt; a example:Box .</p>\n\n<p>/rest/test_object/fcr:acl</p>\n\n<p>&lt;&gt; a webac:Acl .</p>\n\n<p>&lt;#auth1&gt; a acl:Authorization ;<br/>\n    acl:mode acl:Read ;<br/>\n    acl:accessTo &lt;/rest/test_object&gt; ;<br/>\n    acl:accessToClass example:Box ;<br/>\n    acl:agent \"Bob\" ;<br/>\n    acl:default &lt;/rest/test_object&gt; .</p>\n\n<p>Any child (ie. /rest/test_object/child) would see an effective Acl of</p>\n\n<p>&lt;&gt; a webac:Acl .</p>\n\n<p>&lt;#auth1&gt; a acl:Authorization ;<br/>\n    acl:mode acl:Read ;<br/>\n    acl:accessTo &lt;/rest/test_object/child&gt; ;<br/>\n    acl:accessToClass example:Box ;<br/>\n    acl:agent \"Bob\" .</p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p>Therefore it is probably better to disallow having both acl:accessTo and acl:accessToClass in the same authorization.</p>",
